{"schema_version":1,"id":"targets","title":"What counts as EC: target definitions and Adama","generated":"2026-10-30T18:12:57Z","generated_from":"gallery/data/export_ml.py","file":"ml/targets.json","text":{"finding":"Only the target changes. On the lowest-OC/EC cohort FTIR predicts total carbon best (held-out-site R² 0.897) and EC under the transmittance convention worst (EC_TOT 0.764 vs EC_TOR 0.870); without composition selection EC_TOT collapses (R² 0.182). The OC/EC split itself is unlearnable out of site (EC/TC share R² 0.007) (ftir_42). The pyrolysis correction Δ is predictable on the cohort (R² 0.770), and composing EC_TOR − Δ does no worse than a direct EC_TOT model (R² 0.774 vs 0.764): EC_TOT is hard because of the carbon, not the correction (ftir_48). At Adama, EC_TOT is 19 % below EC_TOR, the FTIR carbon sum is 0.51× thermal TC, the implied MAC is 16.5 m²/g against EC_TOR (unflagged median) (ftir_41), and the locked 800 + AIRSpec calibration reads 1.40× EC_TOR where the deployed one reads 0.69× (ftir_44). Five pairs, one month, two flagged."},"sources":[{"table":"target_definition_summary","rows":8,"notebook":"ftir_42_target_definition_experiment","read":"executed notebook output","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_42_target_definition_experiment.ipynb","cell":"summary.to_csv(OUT / 'target_definition_summary.csv'"},{"table":"tc_direct_vs_summed","rows":2,"notebook":"ftir_42_target_definition_experiment","read":"executed notebook output","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_42_target_definition_experiment.ipynb","cell":"sum_table.to_csv"},{"table":"addis_by_ec_convention","rows":4,"notebook":"ftir_42_target_definition_experiment","read":"executed notebook output","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3/ftir_42_target_definition_experiment.ipynb","cell":"addis_table.to_csv(OUT / 'addis_by_ec_convention.csv'"},{"table":"pool_ratio","rows":1,"notebook":"ftir_42_target_definition_experiment","read":"executed notebook output (printed)","path":"research/ftir_ec_phase3